msgid "Languages: extracted, rendered, and RTL"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn:54
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Marks, palettes and art against the instance's own declaration rather than a remembered style. The question a downstream folio makes sharp: would this instance inherit something it did not choose?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn:83
#. Diagram label
msgid "none"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn:70
#. Diagram label
msgid "Raise findings before the assets land"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn:28
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reviewer"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn:17
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reviewing GRAPHICAL ASSETS AS THEY ARE INGESTED — accessibility, branding, languages — in the context of the website or app design they are for, to determine what the graphical assets and the UI are going to be. AT INGESTION ONLY: it is called from `ingest-theme.bpmn`. WHY THE MOMENT MATTERS. Reviewed after a build, a finding is a defect in something shipped. Reviewed at ingestion, the same finding is a decision about what the assets WILL be, taken while it is still cheap. The question the review asks is unchanged; the object it asks it of moved upstream, and so did the cost of the answer. There is no role-to-theme mapping — theme choice remains an authoring judgement, per note — so nothing here checks a binding. What gets reviewed is the ingested art in its design context."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn:68
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer's judgement of the ingested assets in their design. `yes` raises findings before the assets land; `none` ends reviewed and the Theme node proceeds."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn:29
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The single point in this process where a person looks rather than a tool measures, reached only after all four agent passes are done — so what this lane judges is the ingested assets as a whole, in the design they are for — not any one axis in isolation. Its finding is the only thing that can send the process to A_RaiseFindings; a clean ingest, a passing accessibility check and a correct branding pass can each be true and still miss what only laying the assets out and looking catches."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn:14
#. Diagram label
msgid "Theme and UI review — at ingestion"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn:46
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Which graphical assets arrived, for which surfaces of the website or app design, in which locales, and at which VIEWPORTS: every surface at a web width and at a mobile width. Read off the ingested artefacts rather than off the intent — a layout the source declares but does not supply is not in the inventory, and a surface the design needs but no asset covers is the one that would ship wrong."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn:81
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
